     {
      "id": "17872061877472528",
      "text": "\ud83d\ude42Thanks for sharing. This question, reminds me of my late mother who once told me that, how much she hates answering the simple question of \u201cHow are you?\u201d when she was struggling with cancer. \n\nAlthough I myself never suffered the same illness she had, deep down, I kind of understand. After all, it is not always easy, to reveal the unpleasant truth about our own life to others. That\u2019s why many of us prefer to use that standard \u201cI\u2019m fine\u201d answer whenever we don\u2019t feel like talking about it. \n\nYou\u2019re right. Our life is not a performance to entertain others. We don\u2019t really owe anyone any explana",
